; regression test: `forall` must be usable -- and, in particular, must not crash --
; without ever `load`ing any theory. Before `forall`/`exists`'s syntax (arity, bindop,
; bool signature) was hard-coded into `initial_kb` (see doc/kurt-soundness.md §1 and
; the "Update, since fixed" note in what used to be §2's "related wrinkle"), the bare
; word `forall` parsed as an ordinary, flatly space-applied symbol with the wrong shape,
; and the very first formula that mentioned it crashed with an uncaught
; `AssertionError` in `remove_outer_forall_quantifiers` -- reachable with nothing more
; than the `use` line below, no `let`, no `load logic` involved at all.
;
; as a bonus, this also demonstrates that forall-elim already happens "for free": no
; explicit rule is needed to get from `forall x A x` to a specific instance `A a`.
bool A
arity A 1
const a
use forall x A x
A a
